## Computing Statistics on a Vec

### The Functions

```xiom
fn find_min(numbers: &Vec[Int]) -> Option[Int] {
  if numbers.len() == 0 { return Option.None; };
  let mut min = numbers.get(0).unwrap();
  let mut i = 1;
  while i < numbers.len() {
    let n = numbers.get(i).unwrap();
    if n < min { min = n; };
    i += 1;
  };
  Option.Some(min)
}

fn find_max(numbers: &Vec[Int]) -> Option[Int] {
  if numbers.len() == 0 { return Option.None; };
  let mut max = numbers.get(0).unwrap();
  let mut i = 1;
  while i < numbers.len() {
    let n = numbers.get(i).unwrap();
    if n > max { max = n; };
    i += 1;
  };
  Option.Some(max)
}

fn average(numbers: &Vec[Int]) -> Option[Int] {
  if numbers.len() == 0 { return Option.None; };
  let mut sum = 0;
  let mut i = 0;
  while i < numbers.len() {
    sum += numbers.get(i).unwrap();
    i += 1;
  };
  Option.Some(sum / numbers.len())
}
```

### Finding the Median

The median is the middle value when sorted. Sort the list, then take the middle element.

```xiom
fn median(numbers: &Vec[Int]) -> Option[Int] {
  if numbers.len() == 0 { return Option.None; };
  let mut sorted = numbers.clone();
  sort(&mut sorted);
  let mid = sorted.len() / 2;
  Option.Some(sorted.get(mid).unwrap())
}
```

### Computing Range

```xiom
fn range(numbers: &Vec[Int]) -> Option[Int] {
  let min_val = find_min(numbers).unwrap();
  let max_val = find_max(numbers).unwrap();
  Option.Some(max_val - min_val)
}
```

